# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Below Ice Mountain" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Willow the "archaeologist"
0	section	Talking to Willow
1	line	Player	Hello there. What are you doing all the way out here?
1	line	Willow	Just... looking around.
1	line	Player	Oh, did you lose something?
1	line	Willow	No... I found something. A door.
1	line	Player	A door? I see doors all the time. What makes this one so special?
1	line	Willow	It's buried beneath a tonne of rocks. Could be the entrance to some ancient ruins...
1	line	Player	Wow! Ancient ruins? Are you an archaeologist or something?
1	line	Willow	Archaeologist? Me? Hmm...
1	line	Willow	Of course I am! I'm the greatest archaeologist of our time. The name's Willow! Have you not heard of me?
1	line	Player	I'm afraid I haven't. Are you looking for a way into the ruins?
1	line	Willow	You bet I am, but I don't think there's any other way in.
1	line	Player	Oh dear. Do you have another plan to get in?
1	line	Willow	Potentially, but I won't be able to do it on my own. Nor can I leave the area. If I'm not here to guard the entrance, some other archaeologist might come along and steal the glory from me!
1	line	Willow	Maybe you could give me a hand? There could be untold riches inside the ruins!
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	A chance to uncover ancient ruins doesn't happen every day! Of course I'll help! I'm {player} by the way. How do you plan to get in?
2	line	Willow	The entrance is covered in rocks and rubble - I don't think mining them will work.
2	line	Willow	We'll need something stronger. Who knows what could be inside the ruins. There could be traps, or even monsters!
2	line	Willow	No, I think we'll need to get my old crew...
2	line	Willow	...I mean, excavation team together. But you'll need to convince them to help us. We didn't part on the best of terms.
2	line	Player	What happened?
2	line	Willow	We had a falling out after a, uhm... dig, went wrong.
2	line	Player	Where can I find your old team, and how will they help?
2	line	Willow	To get into the ruins we'll need to blow up all the rocks blocking the entrance.
2	line	Player	That doesn't sound too safe. What if we damage the ruins? Surely it's better to go slower and preserve as much as we can?
2	line	Willow	No! We need to get in there as soon as possible! Burntof the dwarf will do it. He's a master with explosives.
2	line	Willow	From what I can remember, he's a fan of his drink. His favourite pub being the Rising Sun Inn, in Falador - I'd look there first.
2	line	Willow	After we've blown the rocks away, we'll need someone to move all the rubble. Someone strong.
2	line	Player	I could do it! I'm quite strong myself.
2	line	Willow	Ha ha ha! I don't think so. We need a real [strongman/strongwoman] - someone with muscles. An old friend of mine, Checkal, should be able to do all the heavy lifting.
2	line	Player	Oh okay... Where can I find him?
2	line	Willow	Hmm... We had quite a rough falling out when we last spoke, but I heard he's hanging around Barbarian Village.
2	line	Willow	Lastly, if my hunch is correct, this place will be covered in traps. We'll need my pal Marley to disarm them. He's the best thief I know. Been doing it for years.
2	line	Willow	I have no idea where he is these days. But his cousin Charlie in Varrock may know. You should talk to him. He's normally somewhere near the Blue Moon Inn.
2	line	Player	You have a rather interesting group of friends... but if they get us into the ruins, I'm all for it.
2	line	Willow	Good luck. Once you've recruited one of the team, I'll meet them at the entrance. It's on the west side of the mountain.
2	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	Seems like you're in a bit of a pickle. Have fun with that.
2	action	end
