0	section	The Ruins of Camdozaal
0	section	Talking to Willow
1	line	Player	That's everyone gathered. Interesting company for an archaeologist to keep...
1	line	Willow	*Shrugs* How many archaeologists do you actually know?
1	line	Player	Well I-
1	line	Willow	Exactly. So who are you to judge? Anyway, we're all here and ready to break in... Um, I mean excavate... the entrance.
1	line	Willow	Are you ready? Who knows what's inside the ruins?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	I'm ready as I'll ever be. Let's head in.
2	line	Willow	Right, that's everyone gathered. Thank you, {player}, for all your help.
2	line	Player	Oh it was no pro...
2	line	Willow	Okay everyone, we've wasted enough time. Let's crack this door open. Burntof, you're up!
2	line	Willow	Try not to blow the entire mountain up this time...
2	line	Burntof	Yesh ma'am, let'sh get this rock out the way.
2	action	Screen fades to black.
2	line	Burntof	Jusht got to plashe thish here...
2	line	Burntof	... little bit of dyn-*hic*-amite here...
2	line	Burntof	... and there we go!
2	line	Burntof	Now we light the fushe!
2	action	Screen returns to normal.
2	action	Tsssss...
2	line	Burntof	What are you doin' standin' there?!
2	line	Player	What do you mean?
2	line	Burntof	Everyone'sh ran for cover [lad/lass]. You'd best do the shame.
2	line	Player	Wait, what?!
2	line	Burntof	Clock'sh ticking [lad/lass]!
2	action	The player runs off screen, and the rocks blow up, clearing the way to the ruins.
2	line	Marley	Bloomin' 'eck, Burntof!
2	line	Checkal	That was a tad too explosive I think.
2	line	Player	My ears are still ringing!
2	line	Burntof	Quit yer moanin', it did the job didnae it?
2	line	Willow	He's right, the rock's been broken up. Checkal, it's your turn.
2	line	Checkal	Of course ma'am, I will get to work.
2	action	Screen fades to black.
2	action	Checkal sets to work clearing out the rubble...
2	action	Screen returns to normal.
2	line	Checkal	The work is done, Willow. My apologies if it took too long.
2	line	Willow	Don't be sorry, Checkal. Gotta put those muscles to use somehow.
2	line	Willow	Alright Marley, in you go. Let us know if you find anything.
2	line	Marley	Right, in I go. Wish me luck {player}.
2	line	Player	Try not to die...
2	action	Cutscene shifts to Marley, inside the ruins.
2	line	Marley	Right, let's see what hidden surprises you have in store for me.
2	line	Marley	Hmm...
2	action	Marley disables a trap.
2	line	Marley	That would have been nasty.
2	line	Marley	Is that it? I thought this place would be better protected.
2	action	Marley avoids a tripwire.
2	line	Marley	Now to disarm it...
2	line	Marley	Maybe this will work?
2	line	Marley	That got it!
2	line	Marley	Alright guys! It's safe to come in! I think...
2	action	Screen fades to black; the player and everyone are now inside the ruins.
2	line	Player	Wow, this place is amazing. I can't believe this was hidden away.
2	line	Player	I wonder how long it's been left untouched for.
2	line	Willow	You're impressed? There's nothing here but dust and fallen rocks.
2	line	Burntof	Yaaa*hic*aawn
2	line	Player	You don't find it exciting? As an archaeologist, I thought you would be thrilled at this discovery?
2	line	Willow	Thrilled? What's there to be excited about? I don't see any gold, diamonds, rare gems or piles of lost treasure!
2	line	Burntof	Hmm...
2	line	Player	It's not about the money though, right? We've potentially discovered the long lost ruins of an ancient civilisation!
2	line	Willow	Of course it's about the money. It's always been about money, you fool.
2	line	Player	I don't understand...
2	line	Willow	We're not a team of archaeologist, you idiot. We're grave robbers looking for their next score.
2	line	Burntof	Theshe markings look familiar...
2	line	Player	So this entire time, you've just been using me to help break into these ruins in hopes of finding someone else's treasures.
2	line	Willow	Yep, and you were surprisingly easy to convince. I'll admit, you have been a tremendous help, {player}.
2	line	Willow	But your usefulness has come to an end I'm afraid. I can't simply let you leave here.
2	line	Player	Why not?
2	line	Willow	I can't risk you running to the authorities and telling them about our little gang. We're wanted in quite a few large cities across Gielinor.
2	line	Burntof	I've sheen thish before...
2	line	Willow	I'm afraid this is the end of the road for you, {player}. This ruin is about to become your tomb.
2	action	Burntof steps on a tile, setting something off.
2	line	Burntof	*hic* Woops...
2	line	Willow	What was that noise?
2	line	Burntof	Uh... it wasn't me!
2	action	The ground shakes.
2	line	Willow	Whats happening?!
2	action	The ground stops shaking.
2	line	Willow	It feels like the quaking has finally stopped...
2	action	The rocks by the big doors come to life, becoming an Ancient Guardian.
2	line	Willow	Holy Zamorak! What is that thing?! Checkal, take it down!
2	line	Checkal	I'm a muscle man, not a fighter.
2	line	Marley	I think we should get out of here, Willow!
2	line	Willow	You're right, Marley. Burntof, we're leaving!
2	line	Player	I can't believe they ran so quickly. I suppose I should take care of this thing.
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I need a little bit more time to prepare.
2	line	Willow	Hurry up then! We've waited long enough.
2	action	end
