0	section	Post-quest dialogue
0	section	Ramarno
1	line	Player	Wow. I honestly didn't expect to see a dwarf in these ruins.
1	line	Ramarno	I can't believe it...
1	line	Player	Yeah, exactly.
1	line	Ramarno	It's been so long since I've heard another person's voice.
1	line	Ramarno	How did you find me?
1	line	Player	To be honest, it was all a bit of an accident.
1	line	Ramarno	What do you mean?
1	line	Player	There was a gang of... well, I thought were archaeologists, but it turned out they were grave robbers.
1	line	Player	I helped them clear the entrance to these ruins and we worked our way inside, only to wake up a monster! They ran off and left me to defeat it.
1	line	Ramarno	That wasn't a monster...
1	line	Player	Well it looked menacing enough!
1	line	Ramarno	That was one of the guardians of this once great city.
1	line	Player	City?
1	line	Ramarno	Yes! Camdozaal, home of the Imcando Dwarves.
1	line	Ramarno	These halls once bustled with life, but that was a long time ago. I'm the only one left now. The name's Ramarno.
1	line	Player	Well Ramarno, I'm {player}, and you have me at a loss for words! I'd have never even imagined there would be a whole city down here.
1	line	Ramarno	Not much of a city anymore, I suppose.
1	line	Player	I guess I didn't help with that. Sorry about breaking into your home and killing your guardian.
1	line	Ramarno	We have plenty more. No real harm done. That said, I do think I might have a way for you to make up for it. There'll likely be something in it for you as well.
1	line	Ramarno	My workshop is just north of here. Meet me there and we'll talk further.
1	action	Ramarno departs for his workshop.
1	action	end
0	section	Using any item on Ramarno
1	box	Ramarno still looks shocked. Perhaps you should talk to him first.
1	action	end
0	section	Willow
1	line	Player	So this is where you scampered off to after the monster awoke?
1	line	Willow	Look {player}, it was a simple misunderstanding, that's all...
1	line	Player	Oh really? You threatening to kill me was just a misunderstanding?
1	line	Willow	Things got a little heated down there, but we all made it out alive, right?
1	line	Player	Barely... I had to defeat that monster on my own!
1	line	Player	What are you doing out here, anyway?
1	line	Willow	We thought you'd rat us out to the authorities, so we came out here to hide.
1	line	Willow	Plus, we heard there are some sealed tombs in the desert that haven't been touched in hundreds of years...
1	line	Player	Ah, of course... scoping out your next grave to rob.
1	action	end
0	section	Checkal
1	line	Checkal	{player}, I am so glad to see you are safe.
1	line	Player	Hello, Checkal. Why didn't you tell me about Willow?
1	line	Player	I thought we were friends...
1	line	Checkal	I am sorry {player}. I do respect you and your love for the muscle. But sadly I needed the money. These muscles don't pay the bills on their own.
1	line	Player	Oh, I understand...
1	line	Checkal	Please do not let this incident divert you from your path of becoming a [strongman/strongwoman]! I truly believe in you.
1	action	end
0	section	Burntof
1	line	Player	How you holding up Burntof? Must have had quite the fright when you woke that monster.
1	line	Burntof	You're right [lad/lass]. It did give me a little fright.
1	line	Burntof	But I saw some interesting things down in the ruins...
1	line	Player	What do you mean?
1	line	Burntof	Some of the markings on the wall look very familiar to me. I've seen them before.
1	line	Player	Well, when I defeated the monster, an Imcando dwarf opened the barred door...
1	line	Burntof	An Imcando dwarf! I thought they were all but extinct! You've found something truly amazing {player}!
1	line	Burntof	I wish I had a drink to celebrate, but this desert is bone dry.
1	action	end
